WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.520
How does a cell decide it can afford to grow?

2
00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:07.760
Growth is expensive.

3
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.900
Making protein uses amino acids and much of a cell's ATP.

4
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:18.800
So a kinase called mTOR, inside a complex named mTOR C1, asks two questions.

5
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:22.940
In the standard model, it switches on only when both get a yes.

6
00:00:23.833 --> 00:00:26.813
The first question: has the body said grow?

7
00:00:27.553 --> 00:00:29.533
A growth factor switches on Akt.

8
00:00:29.973 --> 00:00:35.353
Akt phosphorylates a protein of the TSC complex, which takes the complex out of

9
00:00:35.353 --> 00:00:42.073
action. The TSC complex is a GAP, an off switch for a small GT -Pase called Rheb.

10
00:00:42.553 --> 00:00:44.653
So Rheb stays loaded with GTP.

11
00:00:45.493 --> 00:00:49.553
Rheb with GTP is the direct activator of mTOR -C1.

12
00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:53.427
The second question: are there amino acids?

13
00:00:53.927 --> 00:00:56.967
How cells sense amino acids was unknown.

14
00:00:57.407 --> 00:01:00.467
The link was the Rags, small GT paces.

15
00:01:00.967 --> 00:01:04.467
They do not raise the kinase activity of mTOR -C1.

16
00:01:04.827 --> 00:01:10.387
They move it. Without amino acids, mTOR -C1 stays spread through the cytoplasm.

17
00:01:10.907 --> 00:01:15.447
With them, it gathers on the surface of the lysosome, the cell's acidic digestive

18
00:01:15.447 --> 00:01:19.007
compartment. That surface is where it is thought to meet Rheb.

19
00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:24.790
Rheb with GTP can activate only a complex that has been brought to it.

20
00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:27.450
Growth factors set whether Rheb is on.

21
00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:32.890
Amino acids set delivery, and losing them also calls TSC to Rheb.

22
00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:34.850
This is an AND gate.

23
00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:40.690
With both, mTOR -C1 acts on proteins that control the first step of making protein.

24
00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:45.370
With no growth factor, Rheb is off, so the complex stays off.

25
00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:50.390
With no amino acids, the complex leaves the lysosome and stays off.

26
00:01:51.183 --> 00:01:52.783
A third gauge reads energy.

27
00:01:53.163 --> 00:01:58.023
A healthy cell keeps ATP nearly constant, so ATP is a poor alarm.

28
00:01:58.563 --> 00:02:04.943
AMP moves most. With round numbers, when ATP falls by a tenth, AMP rises almost

29
00:02:04.943 --> 00:02:09.023
fourfold. So the kinase AMPK reads AMP.

30
00:02:09.423 --> 00:02:13.463
Once on, AMPK makes the TSC complex more active.

31
00:02:13.463 --> 00:02:15.983
That drains Rheb of GTP.

32
00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:20.203
It also phosphorylates Raptor, which inhibits mTOR -C1.

33
00:02:20.863 --> 00:02:24.803
Energy can veto growth, even when growth factors and amino acids are present.

34
00:02:25.633 --> 00:02:27.073
You can now predict a cell.

35
00:02:27.613 --> 00:02:31.213
When fed, every input says yes, and protein synthesis runs.

36
00:02:31.833 --> 00:02:36.973
With no amino acids, mTOR -C1 leaves the lysosome, and translation slows.

37
00:02:37.633 --> 00:02:40.573
With no energy, AMPK switches on.

38
00:02:41.013 --> 00:02:45.013
It shuts mTOR -C1 off, even when everything else is present.

39
00:02:45.013 --> 00:02:50.113
Keep this rule: two yeses to grow, and low energy can veto them.
